# Git Merge Conflict Resolution Hands-on Lab

Objective:
To learn how to create a merge conflict, resolve the conflict manually, update the .gitignore file, and merge the branch successfully.

Prerequisites:
Git installed
GitHub account
Git Bash
Notepad++
Existing GitDemo repository

Procedure:

Step 1: Checked whether the main branch was in a clean state.
Command:
git status

Step 2: Created a new branch named GitWork.
Command:
git branch GitWork

Step 3: Switched to the GitWork branch.
Command:
git switch GitWork

Step 4: Created hello.xml in the GitWork branch.
Command:
echo "<message>Hello from GitWork branch</message>" > hello.xml

Step 5: Updated the contents of hello.xml.
Command:
echo "<message>Hello updated from GitWork branch</message>" > hello.xml

Step 6: Checked the repository status.
Command:
git status

Step 7: Added the file to the staging area.
Command:
git add hello.xml

Step 8: Committed the changes in GitWork.
Command:
git commit -m "Added hello.xml in GitWork branch"

Step 9: Switched back to the main branch.
Command:
git switch main

Step 10: Created hello.xml in the main branch with different content.
Command:
echo "<message>Hello from main branch</message>" > hello.xml

Step 11: Added the file to the staging area.
Command:
git add hello.xml

Step 12: Committed the changes in the main branch.
Command:
git commit -m "Added hello.xml in main branch"

Step 13: Viewed the commit history.
Command:
git log --oneline --graph --decorate --all

Step 14: Compared the differences between the branches.
Command:
git diff main..GitWork

Step 15: Visual comparison using P4Merge was not performed because P4Merge was not installed.

Step 16: Merged the GitWork branch into the main branch.
Command:
git merge GitWork

Step 17: Opened hello.xml and resolved the merge conflict manually by removing the conflict markers and keeping the required content.

Step 18: Added the resolved file to the staging area.
Command:
git add hello.xml

Step 19: Committed the resolved merge conflict.
Command:
git commit -m "Resolved merge conflict in hello.xml"

Step 20: Updated the .gitignore file to ignore backup files.
Command:
notepad++ .gitignore

Added the following entry:
*.orig

Step 21: Added the updated .gitignore file.
Command:
git add .gitignore

Step 22: Committed the updated .gitignore file.
Command:
git commit -m "Updated gitignore for backup files"

Step 23: Listed all available branches.
Command:
git branch -a

Step 24: Deleted the merged branch.
Command:
git branch -d GitWork

Step 25: Viewed the final commit history.
Command:
git log --oneline --graph --decorate

Step 26: Checked the repository status.
Command:
git status

Step 27: Pushed the latest changes to the GitHub repository.
Command:
git push

Result:
Successfully created a merge conflict, resolved the conflict manually, updated the .gitignore file to ignore backup files, merged the branch into the main branch, deleted the merged branch, verified the repository status, and pushed the final changes to the GitHub repository successfully.

